     "parts": [
      "If you already have the phone in your hand, the **fastest way** is:\n\n### Method 1: Check in Settings\n1. Open **Settings**\n2. Scroll to **About phone**\n3. Look at:\n   - **Model name** (Galaxy S21, S21 Ultra, S22, S22 Ultra)\n   - **Model number** (SM-xxxx) citeturn0search3turn0search10\n\n### Common Samsung Model Numbers\n\n| Phone | Model Number |\n|---------|---------|\n| Galaxy S21 | SM-G991 |\n| Galaxy S21+ | SM-G996 |\n| Galaxy S21 Ultra | SM-G998 |\n| Galaxy S22 | SM-S901 |\n| Galaxy S22+ | SM-S906 |\n| Galaxy S22 Ultra | SM-S908 | citeturn0search10turn0search7\n\n---\n\n### Method 2: Identify by Camera\n\n#### S21 / S22 (Normal)\n- 3 rear cameras\n- Camera island blends into the metal frame\n\n#### S21 Ultra\n- 4 rear cameras + laser sensor\n- Large camera bump\n- Rounded corners\n\n#### S22 Ultra\n- Looks like a Galaxy Note\n- Square corners\n- Individual camera lenses (no camera island)\n- Built-in S Pen slot citeturn0search7turn0search4\n\nimage_group{\"aspect_ratio\":\"16:9\",\"query\":[\"Samsung Galaxy S21 rear\",\"Samsung Galaxy S21 Ultra rear\",\"Samsung Galaxy S22 rear\",\"Samsung Galaxy S22 Ultra rear\"]}\n\n### Method 3: Dial Code\nOpen Phone app and dial:\n\n`*#1234#`\n\nSamsung usually shows model information.\n\n---\n\nPartner, if you send **a photo of the front and back of the phone**, I can usually identify whether it's **S21, S21+, S21 Ultra, S22, S22+, or S22 Ultra** within a few seconds."
     ]
