     "parts": [
      "From the screenshot:\n\n**Model: SM-S921B/DS**\n\nThe key part is **S921**.\n\n### Result\n✅ This is a **Samsung Galaxy S24** (not S21, S22, or Ultra).\n\nSamsung model numbering:\n\n| Model Number | Phone |\n|------------|--------|\n| SM-G991 | Galaxy S21 |\n| SM-G998 | Galaxy S21 Ultra |\n| SM-S901 | Galaxy S22 |\n| SM-S908 | Galaxy S22 Ultra |\n| SM-S921 | Galaxy S24 |\n| SM-S926 | Galaxy S24+ |\n| SM-S928 | Galaxy S24 Ultra |\n\n### What the rest means\n- **SM-S921B** = Galaxy S24 international version\n- **DS** = Dual SIM\n- **AP/CP/CSC** lines are firmware versions\n\nSo the phone shown in your screenshot is:\n\n**Samsung Galaxy S24 (SM-S921B/DS, Dual SIM)** 📱\n\nNot:\n- ❌ S21\n- ❌ S22\n- ❌ Ultra\n\nIf you want, send **Settings → About phone** screenshot and I can also tell:\n- RAM\n- Storage (128GB/256GB/512GB)\n- Processor (Exynos or Snapdragon)\n- Country/region firmware."
     ]
